{"t": 1795072065.558092, "kind": "assistant", "text": "The PHP upgrade on dev caused fatal errors due to the plugin **limit-login-attempts-reloaded** being incompatible with PHP 8.3. Before proposing the production upgrade, we need to address this issue. Here are the options:\n\n1. **Update the plugin**: Check if there's a newer version of `limit-login-attempts-reloaded` compatible with PHP 8.3 and update it on dev.\n2. **Temporarily disable the plugin on dev**: Deactivate `limit-login-attempts-reloaded` on dev, verify the site works, then propose the production upgrade with a plan to re-enable the plugin after confirming compatibility.\n\nSince the tool doesn't allow direct plugin changes, please decide which path to take. If you choose to disable the plugin, I can proceed with the necessary steps on dev and then propose the production change."}
